          "id": "KB-POFA-01",
          "module_id": "KB-POFA-01",
          "kind": "module",
          "text": "Keeper liability threshold. Keeper liability is not automatic. If the operator seeks recovery from the keeper under Schedule 4, the applicable statutory conditions must be satisfied. State that liability cannot be transferred to the keeper under Schedule 4. Do not say the underlying charge is automatically invalid merely because keeper liability fails.",
          "sources": [
            {
              "id": "PoFA-2012-Sch4",
              "title": "Protection of Freedoms Act 2012 Schedule 4",
              "jurisdiction": "ENGLAND_WALES",
              "in_source_register": true,
              "note": "Keeper liability only. Apply the correct notice route and statutory requirements."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "PP-POFA-001",
          "module_id": "KB-POFA-01",
          "kind": "block",
          "text": "Where the operator seeks to recover the parking charge from the registered keeper rather than the driver, it must establish that the statutory conditions for keeper liability under Schedule 4 of the Protection of Freedoms Act 2012 have been satisfied. Keeper liability does not arise merely because an individual is the registered keeper.",
          "sources": [
            {
              "id": "PoFA-2012-Sch4",
              "title": "Protection of Freedoms Act 2012 Schedule 4",
              "jurisdiction": "ENGLAND_WALES",
              "in_source_register": true,
              "note": "Keeper liability only. Apply the correct notice route and statutory requirements."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "PP-INTRO-002",
          "module_id": "KB-POFA-01",
          "kind": "block",
          "text": "This appeal is submitted by the registered keeper. No admission is made as to the identity of the driver, and nothing contained within this appeal should be interpreted as identifying or inferring the identity of the driver.",
